WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.719
These standing stones are enormous
and made of solid granite.

00:00:03.719 --> 00:00:06.259
When you're near them,
they are genuinely impressive and imposing,

00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:10.389
the sort of thing that makes you wonder how
ancient people ever managed to raise them up,

00:00:10.389 --> 00:00:16.420
and to place them so precisely that
they act as an astronomical calendar.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.700
These particular stones don't
make you wonder that, though.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.300
Because these are the
Georgia Guidestones, in the USA,

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:26.560
and they were put up in 1980 by modern people
with modern equipment.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.690
They are not a theme park
fiberglass replica, though,

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:33.809
they're more than a hundred tons of rock and
they are built to last.

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:35.760
Inscribed on them in eight languages are

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.489
what seem to be rules for a
future post-apocalyptic civilisation,

00:00:39.489 --> 00:00:41.960
the sort of thing that maybe seemed
like a reasonable way

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.760
to send a message to the far distant future

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.879
in an era when the Cold War was looking dicey

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:51.469
and Ronald Reagan's finger was
very close to the nuclear button.

00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:54.510
The person or people who paid for these stones
stayed anonymous,

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:59.979
so no-one knows if they were actually intending
to troll conspiracy theorists.

00:00:59.979 --> 00:01:03.649
Maybe they really were just hoping to create
a modern Stonehenge,

00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:06.190
something that could be taken as
a set of principles

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:11.490
for the world's population to follow as we
recovered after an apocalypse.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:15.980
This might seem like a reasonable purchase,
even altruistic from a certain perspective,

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.790
if you're the sort of person who writes a
story in your head that says,

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:23.880
yes, I'll be dead in a nuclear fireball,
but if civilization survives,

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:27.810
perhaps someone will come across these,
perhaps some language will have survived,

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:33.480
perhaps I will have influenced the entire
path of a civilization to come.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.420
It'd take a lot of money and a lot of ego,

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.930
but then, it was America in the 1980s,

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:43.250
so perhaps we should just be surprised that there
aren't more stones like this all over the place.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:46.110
Imagine a dozen different monuments,
all with different rules,

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:48.930
and all being followed by a
different group of survivors.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:51.570
I don't normally speculate like this in videos,

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.970
but these stones inspire some
pretty good stories.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:57.050
And some pretty bad ones, too.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:01.780
Because like I said, if you wanted to
inflame conspiracy theorists?

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:05.600
Building a modern Stongehenge,
that acts as an astronomical calendar,

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.729
with ten commandments
inscribed upon it,

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:12.150
one of which says that you should
"guide reproduction wisely",

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.060
and another says that it'd be
a really good idea

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:18.400
to have a world population under 10%
of what it currently is,

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.920
and doing all that while hiding your identity?

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.880
Yes, I can see why that might make people with
a slightly tenuous grasp on reality a bit angry.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.540
All the best secret societies, after all,

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:32.140
do put up giant monuments
advertising their goals for the world.

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:35.240
Maybe someday we will know the real reasons
behind these stones:

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.280
but until then there's a rule of thumb
called Occam's Razor.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:41.030
The simplest solution tends to be
the correct one.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:45.930
And a rich person who saw Stonehenge and thought
"I want one of those"

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.080
is a pretty simple solution.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.520
♪ [a faint recording of the US Marine Band playing
"Nearer, My God, To Thee"] ♪

